{
  "test": "Fixed-window separation of Mandarin three-way overlaps at one far-field microphone, followed by enrollment-based A/B/C labeling.",
  "interpretation": "Energy alignment is squared waveform correlation over the reference three-way activity. The strict test requires each speaker to meet the stated alignment threshold AND preserve target gain over at least 96% of active time. The window and the presence of three voices are given to the separator. These results do not measure diarization, transcription, naturally simultaneous speech, or end-to-end meeting performance.",
  "data": "AliMeeting disjoint turn replay captured on array channel zero; one development and one confirmation physical room. Each clip spans 1.536 s with disjoint donor utterances. Four nominal levels (0,-6,-12,-20 dB) repeat twice; identities rotate.",
